1
00:00:48,850 --> 00:00:52,970
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:55,960
[Episode 26]

3
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:01,850
Well, well.

4
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:04,650
You're even calling in hookers now.

5
00:01:06,210 --> 00:01:07,210
Keep this up,

6
00:01:07,210 --> 00:01:08,350
and you won't even remember

7
00:01:08,350 --> 00:01:09,410
your own name, huh?

8
00:01:09,810 --> 00:01:12,010
I was just keeping clients happy for you

9
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:13,590
and playing along.

10
00:01:16,289 --> 00:01:17,970
So should I thank you,

11
00:01:18,010 --> 00:01:18,789
Mr. Liu?

12
00:01:21,330 --> 00:01:22,510
Then what about me?

13
00:01:24,350 --> 00:01:27,450
Are you playing along
with that dying wife of yours,

14
00:01:28,530 --> 00:01:30,640
or are you playing along with me?

15
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:49,950
When it comes to acting,

16
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:51,910
no one can outdo you.

17
00:01:54,850 --> 00:01:55,900
Best Actress.

18
00:02:25,710 --> 00:02:28,270
What about these, Mr. Liu?

19
00:02:33,130 --> 00:02:34,610
Is this enough

20
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:36,870
to buy you for the night?

21
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:34,600
What's wrong?

22
00:03:36,140 --> 00:03:37,280
Nothing serious.

23
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:38,829
Someone must've broken in.

24
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:43,450
Did you lose anything valuable?

25
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:47,290
No.

26
00:03:48,150 --> 00:03:49,120
Just keys.

27
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:50,750
All my keys were taken.

28
00:03:51,950 --> 00:03:53,070
What keys?

29
00:03:54,810 --> 00:03:56,400
Door keys, cabinet keys,

30
00:03:56,430 --> 00:03:57,740
my office keys,

31
00:03:57,760 --> 00:03:59,350
bike keys—all gone.

32
00:04:00,460 --> 00:04:01,800
That's so strange.

33
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:02,740
Nothing stolen,

34
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:03,740
just keys.

35
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:08,980
Probably some brat did it.

36
00:04:12,810 --> 00:04:13,560
Only took the keys?

37
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:14,910
Then it's gotta be a kid,

38
00:04:15,090 --> 00:04:15,690
right?

39
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:18,100
It's fine.

40
00:04:51,270 --> 00:04:52,909
You know who did it,

41
00:04:53,830 --> 00:04:54,450
don't you?

42
00:05:04,570 --> 00:05:05,510
I told you.

43
00:05:05,510 --> 00:05:07,430
Probably some brat did it.

44
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:15,860
Liu Yang.

45
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:20,080
You're out there making money to treat me.

46
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:22,000
Technically,

47
00:05:22,570 --> 00:05:23,870
I have no say in this.

48
00:05:25,390 --> 00:05:27,010
But I hope you'll be careful.

49
00:05:31,860 --> 00:05:32,860
What are you talking about?

50
00:05:32,860 --> 00:05:33,720
Why do I have to—

51
00:05:57,750 --> 00:05:59,480
I should call you Boss Yang now.

52
00:06:00,750 --> 00:06:02,810
Getting a good woman
really changes things.

53
00:06:02,810 --> 00:06:04,170
Got you looking sharp.

54
00:06:10,950 --> 00:06:11,880
What's with you?

55
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,010
I haven't seen you for so long.

56
00:06:13,010 --> 00:06:14,940
How come your tastes have changed?

57
00:06:15,190 --> 00:06:16,360
You don't order girls anymore?

58
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:17,820
Drinking all by yourself.

59
00:06:17,870 --> 00:06:19,750
Why would I order girls?

60
00:06:20,310 --> 00:06:21,930
Am I not enough for you?

61
00:06:21,950 --> 00:06:22,830
Enough.

62
00:06:24,750 --> 00:06:25,950
Dance for me. Come on.

63
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:28,130
Do the cha-cha for me.

64
00:06:28,470 --> 00:06:30,400
Who do you think you are talking to?

65
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:31,950
What are you yelling about?

66
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:37,360
My brother wants to see it,

67
00:06:37,570 --> 00:06:38,960
so I've gotta dance.

68
00:06:38,990 --> 00:06:40,190
Is this the cha-cha?

69
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:41,190
Is this it?

70
00:06:41,190 --> 00:06:41,890
Forget it.

71
00:06:41,890 --> 00:06:44,490
Even if you dare to dance,
I don't dare to watch.

72
00:06:44,740 --> 00:06:45,630
Get out. All of you.

73
00:06:45,630 --> 00:06:47,230
I need to have a word with him.

74
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:55,600
Bro.

75
00:06:57,070 --> 00:06:58,330
Tell me straight.

76
00:06:58,620 --> 00:06:59,390
Is Zhao Changyou's

77
00:06:59,390 --> 00:07:00,240
key with you?

78
00:07:00,810 --> 00:07:01,420
Who?

79
00:07:02,170 --> 00:07:03,490
Your uncle?

80
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:07,160
Playing dumb.

81
00:07:07,370 --> 00:07:08,430
Keep playing dumb.

82
00:07:08,630 --> 00:07:10,250
Come, look at this. Come.

83
00:07:12,810 --> 00:07:13,670
Look familiar?

84
00:07:14,770 --> 00:07:17,740
100% pure natural Siberian tiger penis.

85
00:07:18,660 --> 00:07:19,740
This stuff—

86
00:07:20,310 --> 00:07:22,270
only Zhao Changyou could get it.

87
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:24,770
Do you know how much money I sank

88
00:07:24,770 --> 00:07:26,300
into this batch of goods?

89
00:07:27,570 --> 00:07:28,430
Well, bro,

90
00:07:28,430 --> 00:07:29,830
you're not paying a cent,

91
00:07:30,190 --> 00:07:32,250
and you're gonna pocket what's mine?

92
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:41,600
Let's put it this way.

93
00:07:43,330 --> 00:07:44,710
Suppose you found

94
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:46,520
a bag of money on the street.

95
00:07:47,030 --> 00:07:48,730
Would you want to give it back?

96
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:52,470
That's not right.

97
00:07:53,630 --> 00:07:54,980
Even the song goes:

98
00:07:55,540 --> 00:07:57,300
♪ I found a cent ♪

99
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:58,930
♪ by the roadside ♪

100
00:07:58,930 --> 00:08:02,300
♪ and I handed it to the policeman ♪

101
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:04,100
♪ He took the money ♪

102
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:05,740
♪ and nodded at me ♪

103
00:08:05,890 --> 00:08:07,480
♪ I happily said— ♪

104
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:09,100
"Goodbye, officer."

105
00:08:14,970 --> 00:08:16,030
Stand right there!

106
00:08:17,980 --> 00:08:19,630
Your sister's just a beat cop.

107
00:08:19,630 --> 00:08:21,390
What are you so arrogant about?

108
00:08:22,630 --> 00:08:23,390
You think I've been in Tiecheng

109
00:08:23,390 --> 00:08:24,990
all these years for nothing?

110
00:08:37,130 --> 00:08:38,789
All these years for nothing?

111
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:41,299
Why are you getting so worked up?

112
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:42,880
Come on, let's say—

113
00:08:43,130 --> 00:08:45,060
if you return something you found,

114
00:08:45,290 --> 00:08:47,490
shouldn't there be some kind of reward?

115
00:08:47,790 --> 00:08:49,510
You're all talk.

116
00:08:49,510 --> 00:08:51,770
You just open your mouth and want it back.

117
00:08:51,940 --> 00:08:54,070
That doesn't sit right with me either.

118
00:09:26,030 --> 00:09:27,960
When we go in, what do you call them?

119
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:29,600
Auntie.

120
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:30,460
And?

121
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:32,360
Uncle.

122
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:33,100
Right.

123
00:09:33,270 --> 00:09:35,030
Don't touch anything, okay?

124
00:09:35,030 --> 00:09:37,030
You're a well-mannered kid, right?

125
00:09:38,460 --> 00:09:40,520
Listen to that Northeastern accent.

126
00:09:40,530 --> 00:09:42,100
Guess who'll open the door—
Auntie or Uncle?

127
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:42,960
Auntie.

128
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:44,000
Really?

129
00:09:44,510 --> 00:09:45,390
I guess Uncle.

130
00:09:48,290 --> 00:09:49,370
You got it.

131
00:09:49,370 --> 00:09:50,680
Auntie.

132
00:09:50,770 --> 00:09:53,770
-You're gonna knock Auntie over.
-Qianqian, come in.

133
00:09:56,150 --> 00:09:57,950
Where's Liu Yang? He's not home?

134
00:09:58,270 --> 00:09:59,410
It's the weekend.

135
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:02,720
Come.

136
00:10:03,460 --> 00:10:05,600
How come he's not home
even on weekends now?

137
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:07,720
-Have some candy, Qianqian.
-Don't give her so much.

138
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:08,220
Don't spoil her.

139
00:10:08,220 --> 00:10:08,820
It's fine.

140
00:10:09,340 --> 00:10:11,220
Let's set up a little surprise for her.

141
00:10:11,220 --> 00:10:11,880
Stop!

142
00:10:14,150 --> 00:10:15,290
Don't run. Here I come.

143
00:10:15,290 --> 00:10:17,260
Kid, stop eating candy.

144
00:10:17,390 --> 00:10:18,340
That stuff hurts your throat.

145
00:10:18,340 --> 00:10:19,220
You'll cough at night.

146
00:10:19,220 --> 00:10:21,170
Juan, don't scold the kid.

147
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:22,290
Go ahead and eat.

148
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:25,080
She just eats whatever
she gets her hands on.

149
00:10:25,860 --> 00:10:27,700
What's Liu Yang so busy with every day?

150
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:29,900
Every time I come, I don't get to see him.

151
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:32,200
He's busy.

152
00:10:33,010 --> 00:10:35,270
You're just too easygoing.

153
00:10:35,290 --> 00:10:37,190
If you have any problems, tell me.

154
00:10:37,700 --> 00:10:39,030
I'll beat him up for you.

155
00:11:04,250 --> 00:11:04,860
Juan.

156
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:07,530
What is it?

157
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:11,000
This belt

158
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:12,770
looks quite expensive.

159
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:16,970
Guys don't need to be so particular
about what they eat and wear.

160
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:18,910
I didn't buy it for him.

161
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:22,500
He said it was a fake
on sale at the market.

162
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:28,040
Where did he buy this?

163
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:30,230
The quality feels really good.

164
00:11:30,750 --> 00:11:32,030
I'm gonna get one too.

165
00:11:45,410 --> 00:11:46,580
Hello, Juan.

166
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:48,990
All new stock, just in.

167
00:11:49,360 --> 00:11:50,560
Dirt cheap, just pay.

168
00:11:52,090 --> 00:11:54,130
Juan, your hand's all black
from cracking sunflower seeds.

169
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:56,660
What are you looking for?
I'll find it for you.

170
00:11:57,790 --> 00:11:59,050
Got anything pricier?

171
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:03,100
Here.

172
00:12:03,750 --> 00:12:04,390
Take a look.

173
00:12:04,390 --> 00:12:05,330
Dunhill.

174
00:12:05,530 --> 00:12:06,620
From Guangzhou.

175
00:12:06,790 --> 00:12:08,050
Not a single flaw.

176
00:12:09,050 --> 00:12:09,770
This...

177
00:12:10,530 --> 00:12:11,770
This isn't Dunhill.

178
00:12:11,770 --> 00:12:13,150
It says "danihlm."

179
00:12:13,150 --> 00:12:14,700
Is this real?

180
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:17,570
Juan, you're looking for real stuff here?

181
00:12:17,650 --> 00:12:18,960
You should go to a brand store.

182
00:12:18,960 --> 00:12:21,480
The real ones? How much are those?
Super expensive.

183
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:22,770
Hundreds or even a thousand.

184
00:12:22,770 --> 00:12:24,970
Even the mayor might not wear real ones.

185
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:26,230
How much is this?

186
00:12:26,650 --> 00:12:28,710
Since we're friends, just give me 20.

187
00:12:30,780 --> 00:12:32,910
[Yuhong Square Police Station]

188
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,460
But do you really know him?

189
00:12:39,610 --> 00:12:41,470
Do you know what he does every day?

190
00:12:42,170 --> 00:12:43,340
In just two months,

191
00:12:43,370 --> 00:12:45,550
he went from being penniless

192
00:12:46,360 --> 00:12:47,510
to having a car, a job,

193
00:12:47,510 --> 00:12:48,460
and even a wife.

194
00:12:48,820 --> 00:12:50,030
How did he do that?

195
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:54,050
Ma Xiangqian.

196
00:12:54,290 --> 00:12:55,500
You're taking the night shift alone.

197
00:12:55,500 --> 00:12:56,340
I took leave.

198
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:03,700
I get it. I really do.

199
00:13:03,940 --> 00:13:04,670
Here's the thing, Mr. Fang.

200
00:13:04,670 --> 00:13:06,820
I know you're busy, right?

201
00:13:06,820 --> 00:13:07,600
So I just—

202
00:13:08,250 --> 00:13:08,840
These past couple days

203
00:13:08,840 --> 00:13:11,500
I've been keeping an eye
on this batch of goods for you.

204
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:13,340
Just waiting for you to come take a look.

205
00:13:13,340 --> 00:13:14,770
You can rest easy.

206
00:13:16,240 --> 00:13:16,820
Okay.

207
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:20,480
Let's go, driver.

208
00:13:41,700 --> 00:13:42,240
Hello.

209
00:13:42,630 --> 00:13:43,530
Are you here to

210
00:13:43,530 --> 00:13:45,070
get a room or look for someone?

211
00:13:45,070 --> 00:13:47,070
Do you know that guy who just came in?

212
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:47,860
Sorry.

213
00:13:47,860 --> 00:13:49,150
Whether I know him or not

214
00:13:49,150 --> 00:13:51,010
is the guest's personal privacy.

215
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:53,650
What do you do?

216
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:55,350
[Police Badge]

217
00:13:56,870 --> 00:13:57,530
Po-po...

218
00:13:57,530 --> 00:13:58,860
Po-Police officer.

219
00:13:59,910 --> 00:14:00,970
Well,

220
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:02,640
there's a female boss

221
00:14:02,790 --> 00:14:04,740
who booked a long-term room at our hotel.

222
00:14:04,740 --> 00:14:05,740
Super loaded.

223
00:14:05,860 --> 00:14:07,150
The guy who just went in

224
00:14:07,390 --> 00:14:08,390
is her driver.

225
00:14:08,530 --> 00:14:09,860
He comes every few days.

226
00:14:09,940 --> 00:14:11,200
Once he's in, he stays.

227
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:13,530
Sometimes two or three hours.

228
00:14:13,650 --> 00:14:15,650
Sometimes he even stays overnight.

229
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:16,980
I suppose

230
00:14:16,980 --> 00:14:17,790
they're most

231
00:14:18,370 --> 00:14:19,770
likely having an affair.

232
00:14:21,290 --> 00:14:22,440
Is that guy

233
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:23,770
in some kind of trouble?

234
00:14:25,270 --> 00:14:26,410
Since you're investigating,

235
00:14:26,410 --> 00:14:27,720
I'll grab the key right now.

236
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:28,750
I'll take you to kick the door in

237
00:14:28,750 --> 00:14:30,080
and see what's going on.

238
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:32,440
Why grab a key
if you're gonna kick the door in?

239
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,080
Over there—

240
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:33,670
Is it in the way

241
00:14:33,670 --> 00:14:34,470
if I sit there?

242
00:14:34,510 --> 00:14:35,370
No, not at all.

243
00:14:35,870 --> 00:14:37,130
Sit wherever you like.

244
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:45,080
Officer.

245
00:14:45,940 --> 00:14:48,200
Have a cup of coffee to refresh yourself.

246
00:14:48,940 --> 00:14:49,870
It's completely free.

247
00:14:49,870 --> 00:14:51,600
I can at least treat you to this.

248
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:52,850
Thank you.

249
00:14:52,930 --> 00:14:54,990
I-I'll go get you a fruit platter too.

250
00:14:55,770 --> 00:14:56,830
No need. Thank you.

251
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:58,050
The restroom—

252
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:02,640
J-Just turn left and you'll see.

253
00:15:33,740 --> 00:15:34,650
The car's parked in the back.

254
00:15:34,650 --> 00:15:36,530
We can just walk around to get there.

255
00:15:36,530 --> 00:15:37,170
It's fine.

256
00:15:37,750 --> 00:15:38,480
It's not cold today.

257
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:39,140
I checked

258
00:15:39,270 --> 00:15:41,070
last night's weather forecast.

259
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:50,200
You've really gotten bold, huh?

260
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:51,940
Staying in a room with a woman
all night and not coming out?

261
00:15:51,940 --> 00:15:53,540
What's going on with you two?

262
00:15:53,980 --> 00:15:54,770
Your wife's at home

263
00:15:54,770 --> 00:15:56,290
washing your clothes and cooking for you,

264
00:15:56,290 --> 00:15:57,290
and what do you do?

265
00:15:57,320 --> 00:15:59,130
You're here being your lady boss's lapdog.

266
00:15:59,130 --> 00:16:00,130
Is your belt

267
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:01,240
made of elastic?

268
00:16:01,510 --> 00:16:02,500
It loosens as soon as you see money.

269
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:04,170
All your education was for nothing.

270
00:16:04,170 --> 00:16:06,460
How did the Liu family
produce a piece of trash like you?

271
00:16:06,460 --> 00:16:07,370
This watch of yours,

272
00:16:07,370 --> 00:16:08,520
did she buy it for you too?

273
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:10,290
Costs about half a year
of your salary, doesn't it?

274
00:16:10,290 --> 00:16:11,460
In your life,

275
00:16:11,600 --> 00:16:12,930
you can make less money,

276
00:16:13,010 --> 00:16:14,810
but you can't lose your dignity.

277
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:15,630
Go over there

278
00:16:15,630 --> 00:16:16,840
and tell her it's over right now.

279
00:16:16,840 --> 00:16:17,600
Go right now.

280
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:19,550
Why are you looking at me?

281
00:16:19,550 --> 00:16:20,240
Go!

282
00:16:24,530 --> 00:16:25,630
Our Liu family

283
00:16:25,670 --> 00:16:27,100
has done good deeds for generations

284
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:28,560
and lived with integrity.

285
00:16:28,580 --> 00:16:29,460
If you've done something wrong, it's okay.

286
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:30,260
Fix it in time.

287
00:16:30,270 --> 00:16:31,130
